      "receiptSource": "The original source of this receipt isn\u0027t known. Can you help? \u003Ca href=\u0022mailto:editor@foodsofengland.co.uk?subject=Foods%20of%20England,%20Ovington%20Fruit%20Cake\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Eeditor@foodsofengland.co.uk\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EOVINGTON FRUIT CAKE\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n8 ounces butter\u003Cbr\u003E\n8 ounces flour\u003Cbr\u003E\n8 ounces ground rice or semolina\u003Cbr\u003E\n12 ounces currants\u003Cbr\u003E\n8 ounces castor sugar\u003Cbr\u003E\n3 eggs\u003Cbr\u003E\n2 ounces grated lemon peel\u003Cbr\u003E\nbaking powder\u003Cbr\u003E\nmilk.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nSieve the flour, ground rice and baking powder together. Cream sugar, butter and eggs. Add fruit and flour mixture and enough milk to make a good dough. Place into a well-greased baking tin in a moderate oven for 30 - 40 minutes.\u003Cbr\u003E"
